  "summary": "A vendor-curated Claude Code marketplace of agents, commands, and skills for R-based biostatistics: Bayesian modelling, indirect treatment comparison, tidy R workflows, and clinical trial simulation.",
  "description": "A single-author Claude Code marketplace (Ahmad Sofi-Mahmudi) bundling four plugins covering the core methodology of applied biostatistics in R: bayesian-modeling (Stan, PyMC, JAGS, WinBUGS model authoring and diagnostics), itc-modeling (indirect treatment comparison: pairwise meta-analysis, network meta-analysis, MAIC, STC, ML-NMR), r-tidy-modeling (tidyverse/tidymodels workflows spanning clinical trials, genomics, survival analysis, epidemiology, and pharmacokinetics), and clinical-trial-simulation (power analysis, sample-size determination, group sequential designs, and multiplicity optimisation via simtrial and Mediana). Catalogued here under this registry's bundle admission test (internal project documentation Phase 10): not itself a GA4GH-sponsored project, but a real, publicly discoverable collection whose every plugin is core clinical-trial and biostatistics methodology tooling, not general-purpose or vaguely health-adjacent content. Terms check: the repository carries a real root LICENSE file (MIT, confirmed by direct fetch, not just GitHub's derived metadata), so license is a clean SPDX id rather than the other escape hatch. None of its plugin names collide with this registry's own seeded plugin entries (all ga4gh-* slugs), so ga4gh.members is empty.",
